  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Preventing Human Trafficking and Gender based Violence in Falc&#xf3;n</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The main objective of the proposed intervention is to combat and prevent human trafficking and GBV in the state of Falc&#xf3;n through interventions that focus on i) increasing awareness among the vulnerable groups and people at risk of human trafficking, as well as identified survivors of human trafficking and ii) enhancing capacities of local authorities and civil society organizations within the state to better prevent and respond to human trafficking.  In that line, IOM proposes: a) the organization of awareness raising prevention campaigns including movie screenings and information on GBV and human trafficking response services and reporting mechanisms for vulnerable groups at risk of TiP and GbV, vulnerable communities, returnees, and people on the move; b) the training of civil servants from local authorities and local  NGOs&apos; staff for the detection, identification and derivation of cases and possible cases of trafficking in persons; c) the development a referral pathway document to ensure proper access to case management, assistance and services; and d) the design of a training plan in collaboration with coordination mechanisms such as the UN Protection Cluster Working Group on the Prevention of TiP.</narrative>
  </description>
